{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Recorded one further sourced relationship from the same feature's plumbing without claiming a consensus defect and without spending an execution: the package's own LogCache wrapper forwards the optional MonotonicLogStore interface but defines neither StageCommitIndex nor GetCommitIndex, so it never satisfies CommitTrackingLogStore; since restoreFromCommittedLogs type-asserts that interface and returns ErrIncompatibleLogStore with a warning naming the store's Go type, enabling Config.RestoreCommittedLogs over a cache-wrapped commit-tracking store makes NewRaft fail to start, and the message points at the cache rather than the capable store underneath. Both entries were added as behaviour and fact knowledge with three new source ranges (the wrapper's type and shim, its method set, and the guard in api.go), and the conditions state explicitly that the package documents the requirement, so this is a fidelity gap between the provided wrapper and the provided optional interface rather than an undocumented consensus path. Nothing else changed: the audited question remains explained with its complete account across the five receipts, its gaps closed, and its remaining items recorded as limitations rather than open conjectures.\"}"}}
